{
  "id": "neglect-dyslexia",
  "term": "neglect dyslexia",
  "definition": "Neglect dyslexia is an acquired peripheral reading disorder, usually described after right-brain damage and spatial neglect, in which a person makes reading errors on the left side of written words. It is linked to spatial neglect with altered eye movements and commonly shows left-sided omissions when reading single words or pseudowords.",
